The R package vimcom.plus automatically creates the files that Vim uses for syntax highlight and omnicompletion. You have to install vimcom.plus (http://www.lepem.ufc.br/jaa/vimcom.plus.html) and either run in Normal mode Vim :RpluginConfig (click on R/:RpluginConfig in the Vim menu) or manually put in your Rprofile:

if(interactive()){
    library(vimcom.plus)
}

